<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-przemyslaw-allometric-compound-leaf> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Bilsborough et al. (2011), Barkoulas et al. (2008), Vlad et al. (2014) & Kierzkowski et al. (2019) growing leaf margin PIN1-Auxin-CUC2-RCO feedback loop and serration vs compound leaflet dissection (Arabidopsis thaliana / Cardamine hirsuta (growing leaf margin epidermis, serration teeth, and compound leaflets))",
        "Bilsborough et al. (2011), Barkoulas et al. (2008), Vlad et al. (2014) & Kierzkowski et al. (2019) growing leaf margin PIN1-Auxin-CUC2-RCO feedback loop and serration vs compound leaflet dissection faithfully reproduces Arabidopsis thaliana / Cardamine hirsuta (growing leaf margin epidermis, serration teeth, and compound leaflets) morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/przemyslaw-allometric-compound-leaf-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/przemyslaw-allometric-compound-leaf-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/przemyslaw-allometric-compound-leaf-3> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) 2011-przemyslaw-allometric-compound-leaf.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Arabidopsis thaliana / Cardamine hirsuta (growing leaf margin epidermis, serration teeth, and compound leaflets) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 93.0/100, audit 2026-10-19-allometric-compound-leaf-audit-v2) and the assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8871db0/2011-przemyslaw-allometric-compound-leaf.py> ;
    schema:about "Arabidopsis thaliana / Cardamine hirsuta (growing leaf margin epidermis, serration teeth, and compound leaflets)" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: 3D finite-element adaxial-abaxial lamina thickness mechanics or vascular bundle differentiation inside the rachis",
        "reconstructed_in_script: 1D/2D growing leaf margin Auxin-PIN1-CUC2-RCO reaction-transport and normal contour outgrowth solver verifying Law 1 up-the-gradient PIN1 promotion (error 0.0 < 1e-15) and strong spatial Auxin-CUC2 antiphase (r = -0.9908), Law 2 smooth margin collapse under cuc2-1 loss-of-function (I_D = 0.0120) and cuc2-1D uniform unrepressed CUC2 control (I_D = 0.0250), and Law 3 RCO-driven compound leaflet dissection across 6 genotypes (Pearson r = 0.9983, p = 4.58e-6, RMSE = 0.0169) and 4 developmental stages P3-P6 (1, 3, 5, 7 peaks)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Automated excess-green chromatic + Euclidean distance-transform segmentation of the SHA-256-locked Cardamine hirsuta botanical specimen (`cardamine_hirsuta_compound_leaf_specimen.jpg`, Public domain, 617x992 px) extracting foliage area fraction (0.3668), 32 compound leaflet lobes, perimeter dissection ratio P/(2*sqrt(pi*A)) = 4.0939, and radial tip-to-sinus dissection index I_D = 0.5202 +- 0.0128 SE",
        "reported_in_source: Bilsborough et al. (2011) PNAS 108:3424-3429 interconnected leaf margin feedback loops: Loop 1 (CUC2 promotes PIN1 up-the-gradient polarization rho_{ij} propto (1 + gamma_CUC2 C_i) exp(beta A_j)), Loop 2 (Auxin represses CUC2 transcription C_i = C_max / (1 + (A_i/K_A)^n), restricting CUC2 to inter-tooth sinuses), and Loop 3 (differential normal margin outgrowth v_n(s) = v_0 [A(s)^m/(K_g^m+A(s)^m)] (1 - eta_sinus C(s)) with intercalary tooth insertion when inter-peak distance exceeds lambda_c)",
        "reported_in_source: Vlad et al. (2014) Science 343:780-783 and Kierzkowski et al. (2019) Cell 177:1405-1418 demonstrating that local sinus growth repression by RCO in Cardamine hirsuta converts shallow serrations into deeply incised compound leaflets without changing PIN1/auxin convergence patterning",
        "transfer_boundary: 1D epidermal margin reaction-transport coupled to 2D normal leaf contour outgrowth and 2D botanical specimen contour morphometrics" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "4. Polar Auxin & Turgor Stress" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "III. Phyta (Embryophyta)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Spirals, Veins & Puzzle Cells" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Golden Angle / Auxin Flux" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Angiospermae & Gymnospermae" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Cardamine" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8871db0/2011-przemyslaw-allometric-compound-leaf.py; output: docs/media/allometric_compound_leaf_comparison.png; organism: Arabidopsis thaliana / Cardamine hirsuta (growing leaf margin epidermis, serration teeth, and compound leaflets); checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/8871db0; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1; spec_fingerprint: f7e327f643238b6973cf1043ff1d25ce8c9a027859b313633da11bdc256da7cd; artifact_sha256: 30950e8ff4f1ba0f81bf3b9566ec639fb6cf32e5c5f2525ed0ed4a5ea42a0ab8; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/allometric_compound_leaf/allometric_compound_leaf_reference.json=fa4f9b265dd83379..., datasets/allometric_compound_leaf/cardamine_hirsuta_compound_leaf_specimen.jpg=1c268fecb3660b31..., datasets/allometric_compound_leaf/paper_citations.bib=8245ac5ad5a33db0..., datasets/allometric_compound_leaf/scout_manifest.json=46ea1539febdb312...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-allometric-compound-leaf-audit; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Bilsborough et al. (2011) PNAS 108:3424-3429 interconnected leaf margin feedback loops: Loop 1 (CUC2 promotes PIN1 up-the-gradient polarization rho_{ij} propto (1 + gamma_CUC2 C_i) exp(beta A_j)), Loop 2 (Auxin represses CUC2 transcription C_i = C_max / (1 + (A_i/K_A)^n), restricting CUC2 to inter-tooth sinuses), and Loop 3 (differential normal margin outgrowth v_n(s) = v_0 [A(s)^m/(K_g^m+A(s)^m)] (1 - eta_sinus C(s)) with intercalary tooth insertion when inter-peak distance exceeds lambda_c) | Vlad et al. (2014) Science 343:780-783 and Kierzkowski et al. (2019) Cell 177:1405-1418 demonstrating that local sinus growth repression by RCO in Cardamine hirsuta converts shallow serrations into deeply incised compound leaflets without changing PIN1/auxin convergence patterning; reconstructed_in_script: 1D/2D growing leaf margin Auxin-PIN1-CUC2-RCO reaction-transport and normal contour outgrowth solver verifying Law 1 up-the-gradient PIN1 promotion (error 0.0 < 1e-15) and strong spatial Auxin-CUC2 antiphase (r = -0.9908), Law 2 smooth margin collapse under cuc2-1 loss-of-function (I_D = 0.0120) and cuc2-1D uniform unrepressed CUC2 control (I_D = 0.0250), and Law 3 RCO-driven compound leaflet dissection across 6 genotypes (Pearson r = 0.9983, p = 4.58e-6, RMSE = 0.0169) and 4 developmental stages P3-P6 (1, 3, 5, 7 peaks) | Automated excess-green chromatic + Euclidean distance-transform segmentation of the SHA-256-locked Cardamine hirsuta botanical specimen (`cardamine_hirsuta_compound_leaf_specimen.jpg`, Public domain, 617x992 px) extracting foliage area fraction (0.3668), 32 compound leaflet lobes, perimeter dissection ratio P/(2*sqrt(pi*A)) = 4.0939, and radial tip-to-sinus dissection index I_D = 0.5202 +- 0.0128 SE; transfer_boundary: 1D epidermal margin reaction-transport coupled to 2D normal leaf contour outgrowth and 2D botanical specimen contour morphometrics; does_not_claim: 3D finite-element adaxial-abaxial lamina thickness mechanics or vascular bundle differentiation inside the rachis]" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2019.05.011>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/ng.189>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1015162108>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1248384> ;
